Rain pours down on the memory of the Vrynian rooftop. The sphinx Alhammarret is loud in her ear, and every part of Vraska's body listens with unceasing attention.

"Step off the roof."

She walks to the edge, knowing exactly what she needs to do, is terrified to do it. The drop is far. A groan from the dying Alhammarret behind her roars through her ears. She knows she must jump. She must.

As she leans over the edge of the building, she sees a portal shining far below, a doorway just for her. Vraska lets out a shaking breath of relief. She was commanded to walk, but she was not commanded to aim, and so she aims.

_ Aim for the portal … Aim for the portal … _ She prays with a single foot dangling over the edge of the building, then clenches her teeth as she steps off.

